LibreChat batch 2 (#129): clarifying questions, uploads, long-chat summaries and the sensitive-data filter, in Arabic.
- Clarifying questions: after Skip the record of the question read «إجابتك: The user chose not to answer this
  question.» (the fixed English notice the model receives); it now says «تخطّيت هذا السؤال». The answer's rule and
  indent were on the left in Arabic (border-l, pl), and a few icons and the single-question Submit button used
  physical margins; all logical now. Question, description and answer take their own direction (dir="auto"). An
  answer the filter refuses showed «try again» only; the text now says to remove sensitive data first.
- The sensitive-data filter (`filters` in librechat.yaml) answers with `{error: "content_filter_block", message}` and
  no `code`, so a refused message fell through to the provider renderer: «تعذّر على Qwen إكمال هذا الطلب.
  content_filter_block», blaming the model for our own check. It has its own renderer now, naming what to remove.
- Uploads: errors written as fixed English sentences (size, total size, count, file type in utils/files.ts; «No text
  found in document» and the filter's refusal from the server) and the kind under a file's name («Document»,
  «Spreadsheet»…) showed in English in the Arabic interface; they are translated now (utils/efaiwFiles.ts).
- Summary of a long chat: its box showed the summarizer as «openAI/qwen3.8-flash» (every OpenAI-compatible endpoint
  reports «openAI»), which reads as if the chat had gone to OpenAI; it shows the token count only. Its icon margin
  and action buttons were physical (mr, right), and the text now takes its own direction.

